{% comment %}
  Where the mod sends track submissions.

  Served from the site rather than compiled into the .ksm so it can be rotated
  without shipping a release. If the endpoint ever gets abused, replace the URL
  here, push, and every installed copy picks up the new one within a couple of
  minutes — no player has to update anything.

  Leave `webhook` empty to switch submissions off entirely: the mod hides the
  Submit button and falls back to copy-and-paste.

  A Discord webhook is deliberately the target rather than the GitHub API. The
  mod is public and signed, so any credential inside it can be extracted — a
  GitHub token would hand out write access to the repos, whereas the worst a
  leaked webhook allows is posting into one channel you can delete and replace.
  Players also need no account of any kind, which is the whole point.
{% endcomment %}
